{"type":"text","timestamp":1788352636470,"sessionID":"ses_f9de3a50effeMz6KmFLbj4vnw3","part":{"id":"prt_0621f7e46001IPw7H07Tw65N6S","messageID":"msg_0621e5689001cjQKJM1K9xvQuE","sessionID":"ses_f9de3a50effeMz6KmFLbj4vnw3","type":"text","text":"Now I have a clear picture of the failure. Let me summarize the diagnosis:\n\n**Failure**: `CodegenError: at <source>:20:18` — pointing to `asc2.rsqrt(acc * inv_D + epsilon)` in the kernel.\n\n**Root cause** (from `pyasc-v2-blockers.md:17-19` and `operator-patterns.md:62-67`):\n- `asc2.rsqrt` is a tensor-only unary op that **rejects PlainValue reductions** (scalars from `asc2.reduce_sum`)\n- The fix: broadcast the scalar into an aligned local tensor before applying `rsqrt`\n\n**Fix**: Replace `inv_rms = asc2.rsqrt(scalar)` with `inv_rms_tile = asc2.rsqrt(asc2.full([tile_d], scalar, dtype=asc.float32))`, then use tile-by-tile multiplication in pass 2.\n\nUB impact: +1 f32 tile (4096 B naive, ~6.5 KB with 1.6x factor) → total ~49 KB, well under 253952 B budget.\n\n","time":{"start":1788352626246,"end":1788352636469}}}
